## Context

Found by the 0091 takeover session during the PR A/B merge, reported
2026-09-01: upstream's `tsconfig.json` excludes `tests`, so `npm run
typecheck` never typechecks the test suite. A test importing a symbol that no
longer exists passes typecheck and fails only at runtime — it bit during the
merge of the two prepared droplist branches, where a rename (`HighDf` →
`Prunable`) left a test compiling against a ghost.

The defect class is the familiar one: a gate whose all-clear is
indistinguishable from not looking. Upstream's own contribution bar asks for
`npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` green; the first of the three
silently covers only half the tree.

## Relevant files
- Upstream `tsconfig.json` — the `exclude` entry.
- Upstream `package.json` — the `typecheck` script.

## Actions
1. Verify at current upstream HEAD that the exclusion is still present and
   that a deliberately broken test import passes `npm run typecheck` (the
   positive control — do not trust the report without it).
2. Measure the blast radius: run `tsc --noEmit` over the suite once; the
   exclusion may be hiding accumulated type errors in tests, which changes
   the fix from one line to a cleanup.
3. Decide the upstream form per the measured asymmetry: a one-line fix with a
   clean suite is a contained PR; an exclusion hiding many latent errors is
   design-sized enough to go as an issue he fixes his own way.

## Test
- The positive control in action 1 is the red step: a test file importing a
  nonexistent symbol must fail typecheck after the fix and pass before it.

## Measurement, 2026-09-02

Run at `b05ed69` (v1.12.0) on the fork branch `base-v1.12.0`, TypeScript
5.9.3, vitest 2.1.9, `npm ci` on the committed lockfile. Draft filing body:
[`verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0530.md`](../../verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0530.md).

Two corrections to the premise, neither of which moves the finding: the
fork's `main` is `bb414df` (v1.9.0), not v1.12.0 — `b05ed69` lives on
`base-v1.12.0`, and `tsconfig.json` is byte-identical on both; and the suite
is 101 `.ts` files / 15,754 lines (100 `*.test.ts` plus
`tests/fixtures/epub.ts`), not 102 / 15,907.

**Positive control, both directions.** A ghost import planted in
`tests/config.test.ts` leaves `npm run typecheck` at exit 0 with no output,
indistinguishable from the clean tree, and leaves `npm test` green
(`✓ tests/config.test.ts (28 tests)`). Compiled with tests included, the same
file yields `TS2305: Module '"../src/config.js"' has no exported member
'aGhostSymbolThatDoesNotExist'` and `TS2322: Type 'string' is not assignable
to type 'number'`. Worse than the ticket assumed: vitest does not catch it
either, because under the SSR transform a missing export is `undefined`
rather than an import-time throw, so a ghost fails only when *called* — a
renamed type or a read-but-not-invoked symbol can stay broken indefinitely.

**The lock is double, which is why this survived.** `include` (line 18) and
`exclude` (line 19) each block tests independently: removing `"tests"` from
`exclude` compiles zero test files, and adding `tests/**/*` to `include`
compiles zero test files. Both together, with `rootDir: "src"` (line 8) kept,
gives 100 × TS6059 and no type errors at all — and pollutes the tree under
`npm run build`. No one-line fix exists.

**Blast radius: 204 errors across 37 of 101 test files, zero in `src/`**,
while the suite is green at runtime (923 passing, 7 skipped). 115 of the 204
are `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` applied to test idiom (18 files affected by
nothing else); 53 are untyped `await res.json()` and untyped `vi.fn()` mocks;
5 are genuine fixture drift (`Capabilities.localGroupIds`, added in `116b4aa`
— our own #12 — never propagated to four fixtures explicitly annotated with
the interface; `ToolContext.reopenSearchIndex` the same); 10 point back at
`src`, where `toJSON`/`loadFromJSON` exist on the class and on
`persistence.ts` but not on the `SearchIndex` interface
(`backend.ts:524`). No `@types` package is missing: zero TS2307/TS2304/TS2582.

**Form ruled: issue, not PR.** Three grounds, each measured: no one-line
change does anything; the suite does not type-check clean, so a contained PR
would be a 37-file diff carrying a policy choice in every file; and one
category asks whether `SearchIndex` should expose persistence, which is his
interface to decide. This is the asymmetry GOVERNANCE.md § Form follows the
measured asymmetry names, landing on the design-sized side.

